WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.664
Sometimes walking early in the morning,

00:00:10.664 --> 00:00:13.480
I feel so afraid because it
looks like a peaceful place

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.397
but it is the most dangerous place.

00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:27.120
Here in Kibera we don't think about death

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.412
because it always happens.

00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:38.009
It was not my plan to give
birth into that community.

00:00:48.728 --> 00:00:51.944
I feel so afraid raising my child,

00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:54.277
bad things happening around.

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:06.780
They thought that marriage
was the only solution

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.926
for my life after I gave birth.

00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:14.373
But for me, I had my own thoughts.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.050
You know, when Gabby was five
months I went back to school.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.853
I was still breastfeeding him.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.170
The teacher denied me like,
'you can't go back home.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.880
So if you want to study,

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.967
you have to leave that breastfeeding'.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.880
Gabby used to wake up in the
morning and start crying.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.140
Sometimes you don't have milk.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.780
Sometimes you don't have
even anything to give.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.393
I had to make him suffer
to go back to school.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.770
Kibera is an informal settlement.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.280
We call it sometimes a chocolate
city because of the roofs,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.803
when it's raining, it
looks like chocolate.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.990
Nowadays, I hear people saying

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.760
it's one of the biggest
informal settlements

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.930
in the whole world.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.580
It's very rich in cultures,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.050
in people who come from different tribes

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.123
and from different parts of this country.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.830
And there are so many
people who are all chasing

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.300
good living condition.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.923
They have to work extra hard.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.240
Within Kibera children go through a lot

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.150
that sometimes schools
help them to overcome.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.280
Some children are in very abusive

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.590
domestic living conditions.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.200
And schools used to act
as safe haven for them

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.670
because when they're in school,

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.428
they're bit out of their
chaos that is happening

00:03:20.428 --> 00:03:21.693
for them at home.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.320
Our space, this is an afterschool center.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.970
It's a safe house for children.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.710
So children from different schools

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.620
come here to interact and play together

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.303
and also just be children.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:38.970
We run programs,

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.550
the first one being the arts program.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.763
So we do classical ballet,
modern dance, African dance.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.143
I was born in poverty,

00:04:24.143 --> 00:04:26.160
I never went to school myself

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.763
but I was able to find
myself through dancing.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.800
I loved the discipline
- it calmed me down.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.120
It slowed me down.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.319
It tamed me.

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:39.510
Because it's about the body shape.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.004
And so I use it as the
foundation for every dance we do.

00:04:43.004 --> 00:04:46.712
Because it trains you, your
inner self, it trains your body.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.250
Ballet becomes the core.

00:04:57.747 --> 00:04:58.980
So you find the children,

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.650
they're always present,
with their neck straight

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.840
and their back straight.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.810
And when they train that
when they stay here -

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.253
it's magic what you see.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.070
It gives you confidence.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.550
You can stand in a class
and not know the answer

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.660
and no one will know

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.603
because it gives you
the power of presence.

00:05:23.861 --> 00:05:27.690
I have been dancing ballet for five years.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.163
It really inspired me.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.120
The dance gives me confidence

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.493
and I always feel like
I'm top of the world.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.450
It's a little hard
sometimes when you can't

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.490
get the steps correctly

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.800
but me, I don't always give up.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.503
I always try my best until I get it right.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.750
Sometimes girls face many
challenges in Kibera.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.512
But you have to believe in yourself

00:05:54.512 --> 00:05:57.232
and you have to be strong

00:05:57.232 --> 00:05:59.899
and everything will be possible.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.200
We have a group of students

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.900
coming in from America today

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.880
and they're coming in to just listen to us

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:18.980
and then go back home.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.780
Hi. I'm Mike Wamaya.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:22.770
And I'm a dance teacher

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.800
and also a social worker based in Kibera.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:29.790
So basically, I've been able to redesign

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.100
the mindset of dancing here.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.840
And how we use dance

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.930
because I think dance is about solutions

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.520
to the community problems

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.250
and not about showcase and competition.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.170
My students are able to learn that.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.710
And we've now grown to this
very powerful community here

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.893
where now girls can speak
and girls can shout.

00:06:51.599 --> 00:06:53.712
We run a sexual reproductive health

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.560
and rights program

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.810
that supports mainly adolescent girls

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.000
with access to menstrual products.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.120
But also, training on leadership

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:06.123
and also on teenage pregnancy prevention.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:12.440
In between, we do a lot
of talking and mentorship.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.450
My office, there are always
like open for children

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.330
if you have an issue
that you want to address.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.610
So whatever you have in your mind,

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:24.476
you let us know and we will
all find a solution for it.

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:28.064
We're gonna do a big warm up,

00:07:29.522 --> 00:07:31.017
come to first position.

00:07:33.794 --> 00:07:36.690
And now we're gonna reach to one side.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.175
In.

00:07:38.175 --> 00:07:39.810
Our ballet program

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.480
has a combination of both boys and girls;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.767
a majority being girls.

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:48.186
The girls depend on the
boys to lift them up.

00:07:48.186 --> 00:07:50.040
The girl has to shine.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.500
5, 6, 7, go.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.280
You have to work so hard
to lift that girl up

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.010
and that helps the boys to understand

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.160
that it's actually a
collective responsibility

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.933
in making the women rise.

00:08:06.209 --> 00:08:09.000
Poverty has so many ways of disrupting us

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.960
but good education can
build resiliency in you

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.310
and so my aim is to use dance as a tool

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.400
to make children have
their self-realization.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.260
To make children know who they are

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.450
and what they want for their future

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.583
and that everything is in their hands.

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:40.680
When schools closed the first few months,

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.553
we shut down.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.563
We were not able to sustain the rent

00:08:45.563 --> 00:08:50.190
because we had no funding.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.500
Our one donor, they shifted focus

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.200
into like providing Covid
healthcare equipments

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.550
to their own country.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.870
What do you do?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.280
Everything has to stop.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.670
We struggled so hard to
just keep the space open

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:05.580
because we knew how
important this space was

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.533
for our students.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.630
In Kibera, like people
live on daily basis.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.420
So we wake up, we make the
money to eat on that day

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.100
then we go and sleep.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.160
So if we don't do it even one single day,

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.410
it has a repercussion
at the end of the year.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.350
Majority of our parents, the
ones I directly work with,

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:38.370
they work in middle class people's houses.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.830
And so when the Covid pandemic came in

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:44.673
almost 90% of our parents
lost their income.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.700
Also children used to have
access to a meal in the school

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.590
but now when the schools are not there

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.993
the children were left to no meal at all.

00:09:57.818 --> 00:10:00.960
There were no peer support
groups for the young girls

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.210
so they were way more vulnerable.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.520
I had girls who could
not go into their houses

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.250
when their stepfathers are there

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.960
or the person who is taking care of them

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:10.950
as a father is there

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.750
because they don't feel comfortable.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.500
The male people use it wrongly
and they take advantage of it

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.350
by luring some of these
young girls with a bit

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.060
of money here and there

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.550
and eventually for sexual favors.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.220
And then they dump them and run away.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:32.840
In that Covid period some
of them ended up pregnant.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.590
And so the girls went out and they found

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:37.560
so many other young
girls who are pregnant.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.560
And we started slowly
bringing them into this space.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.363
And one who walked in was Winnie.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.298
I got to know Mike

00:10:48.298 --> 00:10:49.890
when I was five month pregnant.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:50.970
I don't have a home.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.140
I don't have anywhere to go.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.610
I don't have a family.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.900
What can I do?

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.720
Mike told me, 'you can't
think about abortion

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:00.240
and you can't think about
killing yourself anymore.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.650
I'm here to help you.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:02.880
And I'm here to support you.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.847
So take this money and
go and eat something'.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.640
He even called my mom one day.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.653
Started telling her like,
no matter how hard it is,

00:11:11.653 --> 00:11:13.410
I know that in this society

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.550
we need to help each other.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.140
We need to lift each other.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:20.160
So don't worry, Mama Winnie, don't worry.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:20.993
It will be good.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.336
To me, when a girl was pregnant,

00:11:27.336 --> 00:11:30.753
my biggest worry was maternal death.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.530
I reach out, try to talk,

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:37.470
and find help and promise
them that we are together;

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.610
because when they get pregnant

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.163
they get so ashamed of themselves.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:46.440
People would always brand a
teenage mother with failure.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.970
And that should not be the case

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:51.450
because the case should be,
there is a mistake somewhere

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.130
and we need to solve something.

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:56.200
There is actually a
problem with all of us,

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:59.706
you know, with the entire community.

00:11:59.706 --> 00:12:02.430
And I just assured her like you know what,

00:12:03.631 --> 00:12:05.548
we will stick together.

00:12:07.223 --> 00:12:08.580
For me, what I want

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.200
is to go back to school.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.450
Because I've seen how life is hard here.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.720
And without education,
I can't do anything.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.480
One day my hopes will come true.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:23.130
And that's me taking away
my family from that place

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.200
and giving them a better future.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.383
It helps me understand, like
there's still life for me.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.550
The myth and the whole
mindset that we have here,

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.040
that when a girl wakes up,
the first thing they need to

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.980
do is to make sure that
the whole house is clean

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.503
before they're able to even open a book.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.090
That's sad but it is actually

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.460
the reality of the ground here.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.070
The housework is so much, is so enormous

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:58.133
that they don't even have time to study.

00:12:59.387 --> 00:13:02.010
At home the chores that I have

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.160
is to wash the dishes, clean the house

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.733
and wash my uniforms, my
siblings uniforms, yes.

00:13:09.733 --> 00:13:11.820
But I'm the girl.

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:13.512
I'm supposed to do the work.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.340
I study to help my family,

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:22.113
I want to lift my family up.

00:13:23.075 --> 00:13:25.860
And I also want to build
my momma a big house.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:29.313
She makes me believe in
myself that I can do it.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.630
When my mom doesn't have the tuition money

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.220
I always stay at home.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:36.630
So when she get the money,

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.210
she always give me the little she have

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.983
and I always take it to school.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:49.920
The beans is ready,

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.339
we are just want to start cooking porridge

00:13:52.339 --> 00:13:53.172
but the water is, is not...

00:13:55.011 --> 00:13:57.990
We see a lot of outcomes in girls.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.690
We have girls who are now in university

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.790
and initially they never
thought they would get

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.190
anywhere close to university.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.500
I have students who I used
to teach when they were

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.700
very small

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.250
and they now dance in the US.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.630
It opens up doors.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:13.950
So it gives you the pride

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.073
because the moment you
realize who you are,

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.920
nothing holds you back.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:20.753
Nothing.

00:14:20.753 --> 00:14:24.033
I used to hate stirring porridge.

00:14:24.881 --> 00:14:27.060
Like where it was a punishment to me.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.940
Because I'm grown up
now, I know how to stir,

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.290
I feel so happy doing that.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.249
The only person that I've met in my life

00:14:35.249 --> 00:14:37.920
that believes in me, it is only Mike.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.930
And I think my son too.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:41.103
And I, myself.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.560
Michael tells me, 'Never give up.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.360
Never, never give up.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.010
Let us continue with the journey.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.420
It is just a rock.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.330
It is just a distraction in your way'.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.460
My dream is to become a news anchor,

00:14:56.460 --> 00:15:00.090
a mentor, a teacher and
someone who can help others

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.923
in future.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.010
I want to see Gabby having a good future

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.150
and start to make Gabby's
education look very light.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:14.853
And make him feel like
he is someone's child.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.930
The father refused him.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.809
Maybe in future, he will
never ask for that man

00:15:21.809 --> 00:15:22.980
in his life.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.260
He will just ask like, 'where's my mom?

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.280
I want to see my mom.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.100
I want to see that friend of
mine who is called my mom'.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:32.753
Go get porridge.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.500
What I want to do is I'm, I'm creating

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:40.413
a mindset of possibilities.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:45.180
No one will come from somewhere
to solve our problems.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:48.450
We have to face our problems
and solve them by ourselves

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:52.350
because the solution of our
problems lies within us.

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:57.090
So I hope I'm able to influence

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.130
majority of my students to think that way.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.513
And that's my biggest goal.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:06.060
Everyone goes in. Now listen up.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.950
We have our friends.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.530
We gonna do a performance for them.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.020
So we have a production we are doing.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:16.860
We're gonna show you part of
it, which is now called Walks.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:17.987
Yeah .

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:31.920
You thought of a move in your head

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.720
and you come here and we practice it

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.370
and it becomes a very beautiful thing

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.080
that everybody claps for it.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.760
That's innovation.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.100
And when children learn
that from the beginning,

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.553
you can take the whole concept
and translate it into school.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.137
If I didn't know something yesterday

00:16:49.137 --> 00:16:51.510
I would try my level best today

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:54.600
and I want to sit back
and listen and follow

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.400
and when I'm now good at doing it,

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.810
I reach out to somebody else

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:00.540
who I see is not able in doing it

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.910
and show him how I was shown.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.293
And together we are rising.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.700
I always say, I need to save other people.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.470
I need to raise other people.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:12.570
But understand that life,
you have to move on.

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.310
You don't have to cry forever.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:16.410
And you know, the time
that you leave your studies

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.210
and say like, I don't
have to go to school -

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.470
that is the end of your dream.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.330
That is the end of your
benefit in the society

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.790
and that is the start of your problems.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:24.990
I need to tell other people,

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.760
this is the solution that I did

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.173
and you need to do the same.

